  {
   "id": "tower-health-stream",
   "name": "Tower Health Stream",
   "kind": "Streaming",
   "featured": true,
   "summary": "A streaming pipeline that monitors simulated telemetry from 10,192 real Egyptian cell tower locations.",
   "problem": "Telecom teams often learn about a weak tower only after customers complain. I wanted to see how early a streaming pipeline could flag it.",
   "built": "Kafka carries tower events, Flink validates them and detects anomalies in 10 minute windows, a Python service adds live weather to each alert, Iceberg stores history, and Grafana shows the results. Airflow and dbt handle the batch side.",
   "result": "In local tests on Docker it handled about 2,000 events per second and raised alerts in under 150 ms.",
